WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.612
Let’s walk through Population Sentiments.

00:00:02.612 --> 00:00:06.600
Read the published sentiment as audience-specific scenario context.

00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:09.500
Identify who received it, what changed in the narrative

00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:11.300
, and whether the team will respond;

00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:14.150
do not treat sentiment as a hidden score or automatic

00:00:14.150 --> 00:00:15.213
outcome.

00:00:15.213 --> 00:00:18.950
On this slide, compose and review team-specific population sentiment

00:00:18.950 --> 00:00:20.062
updates.

00:00:20.062 --> 00:00:24.225
In practice, publish the intended audience and narrative explicitly

00:00:24.225 --> 00:00:24.325
;

00:00:24.325 --> 00:00:27.325
the update is context, not a hidden score change

00:00:27.325 --> 00:00:27.512
.

00:00:28.010 --> 00:00:31.285
When you are ready, use Open Population Sentiments to

00:00:31.285 --> 00:00:33.223
move to the live surface.

00:00:33.223 --> 00:00:36.010
The guide will not make the workflow decision for you

00:00:36.010 --> 00:00:36.160
.
